BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 669.77 Tm (The costliest trap is buying boards on trust. Shark Scrapper's Asheville near-pallet looked like one lot but held dirties) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 654.55 Tm (likely from customers after the Helen flooding, boards still bolted to metal plates that must come off before weighing,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.32 Tm (and enough mixed grades to produce 19 categories [6XObIp5c91U @ 00:01:09]. Paying a flat mixed-board price for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.10 Tm (that load would have risked getting taken to the cleaners, and the rule that follows is simple: don't ever buy a full) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 608.87 Tm (gaylord box of boards believing they are what they say they are, unless the mixed price reflects the risk [6XObIp5c91U) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 593.65 Tm (@ 00:20:51]. Batteries are a hard stop: Storage Unit Scrapper notes boards with batteries cannot be sent, so batteries) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.42 Tm (and heat sinks come off first, and Shark Scrapper repeats that the battery has to go before selling [4TJbVuWoX3A @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.20 Tm (00:20:35]. Leftover tape is a quieter loss; Storage Unit Scrapper heat-guns it off so boards ship clean and are not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 547.97 Tm (downgraded [4TJbVuWoX3A @ 00:15:37]. Shark Scrapper also admits the bin layout for that job did not work, a real) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 532.75 Tm (bottleneck with more pallets coming from two PC repair clients and a scrapyard. Fix the sort floor before the next pallet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 517.52 Tm (lands, not after.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.30 Tm (Local yard prices move against the scrapper. Storage Unit Scrapper once sold whole laptops to the scrapyard at 98) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.07 Tm (cents a pound and now gets 15 cents a pound locally, while laptops listed on HiBid went for $4 to $5 through a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.85 Tm (business that lists 1,000 items a week there [4TJbVuWoX3A @ 01:11:32]. Labor is the other leak: dirty aluminum) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 456.62 Tm (brings 18 cents a pound, and the time and effort to clean it to pure aluminum is not worth it, the same time logic that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.40 Tm (has the channel skipping MOSFETs [bAvpAOGu8Kw @ 00:06:37]. That channel also sits on a copper tote of about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.17 Tm (100 pounds as money in the bank, betting EVs and data centers keep copper rising [bAvpAOGu8Kw @ 00:30:33]. On) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.95 Tm (the buying side, Shark Scrapper normally charges a 10% sorting fee but may waive it for a new client to build) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 395.72 Tm (goodwill, then plans to teach that client to pre-sort, since even a cursory sort earns the client more [6XObIp5c91U @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 380.50 Tm (00:06:47]. Waiving the fee trades margin for supply, and that supply is fragile: the same client is weighing scrapping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.27 Tm (against repairing because the real money is in repairing. Price every hour of stripping against the current yard sheet, not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.05 Tm (last year's.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.82 Tm (On the instrument side, the failures come from trusting a number without checking what produced it. Data Center MEP) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 319.60 Tm (System shows a meter set to 1200/1 on a 1600/1 CT under-reading by 25%, a generic 1,000-volt DC instruction issued) Tj ET
